---
import CoffeeButton from '../components/CoffeeButton.astro';
import Micro from '../components/Micro.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ISSUES_URL, IN_STORE, SOURCE_URL, STORE_REVIEW_URL } from '../lib/links';

/**
 * The two roads an opinion can take, side by side and both open.
 *
 * This page used to be the far end of the extension's thank-you card: the card
 * asked "is it working?", both answers were a link, and a `rating` in the query
 * string lit one of the two columns below. #45 moved that ask into the
 * extension itself — `components/ReviewAsk.tsx` now draws both roads where the
 * question is asked, so nothing sends a rating here any more and the script
 * that read one has gone with it.
 *
 * What is left is worth keeping as a plain page. It is linked from the footer,
 * it is the address to hand anyone who says "how do I tell you something", and
 * it makes the same point the block in the extension makes: both roads are
 * always visible, because deciding who gets to see the review link on the
 * strength of how they rated you is review gating, and the Web Store's
 * rating-manipulation rules reach it.
 *
 * No script at all now, so it is complete as HTML.
 */
---

<Base
  title="Feedback — Reply AI"
  description="Tell me what is working, or what is not. Two links and an address — nothing is collected."
  noindex
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-16 pt-14">
    <Micro n="01" label="feedback" />

    <h1 class="mt-6 text-[38px] font-semibold leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.03em] sm:text-[46px]">
      Two ways to say it. <span class="text-white/55">Both of them help.</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl border-l-2 border-accent pl-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-white/70">
      The extension reports nothing, ever — there is no rating widget inside it counting anything,
      and nothing about you arrives here by itself. Whichever of the two below fits, thirty seconds
      of it is worth more than any number we could have collected.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-24">
    <div class="grid gap-px border border-line bg-line md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 bg-surface p-7 transition-colors duration-200">
        <span class="micro">it is working</span>
        <h2 class="text-[20px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.015em]">Say so where it counts</h2>
        <p class="text-[14px] leading-[1.65] text-white/70">
          {
            IN_STORE
              ? 'A review on the Chrome Web Store is the only thing that puts this extension in front of other channel owners. It takes a sentence.'
              : 'The store listing is still in preparation, so there is nowhere to review it yet. A star on the repository does the same job in the meantime, and I will put the review link here the day the listing is live.'
          }
        </p>
        <a
          class="btn-secondary mt-auto self-start"
          href={IN_STORE ? STORE_REVIEW_URL : SOURCE_URL}
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          {IN_STORE ? 'Leave a review' : 'Star it on GitHub'}
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 bg-surface p-7 transition-colors duration-200">
        <span class="micro">it is not</span>
        <h2 class="text-[20px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.015em]">Tell me what went wrong</h2>
        <p class="text-[14px] leading-[1.65] text-white/70">
          A bad reply, a button that did not appear, a comment section it could not read — all of
          it is fixable, and none of it is fixable without knowing. An issue is public and gets a
          version number; an email is private and gets an answer.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a class="btn-secondary" href={ISSUES_URL} rel="noreferrer">Open an issue</a>
          <a class="btn-ghost" href="/contact?from=feedback">Write to me</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-start gap-4 border border-line bg-surface p-7">
      <span class="micro">or nothing at all</span>
      <p class="max-w-xl text-[15px] leading-[1.7] text-white/70">
        The extension is free, unlimited, has no account and no upsell, and it stays that way
        whichever button you pressed. If you would rather say thank you in the other currency, the
        coffee button is here — and it buys nothing, changes nothing, and unlocks nothing. That is
        the point of it.
      </p>
      <CoffeeButton />
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-[14px] text-white/45">
      Back to <a class="text-white/70 underline decoration-line-hi underline-offset-4 hover:text-white" href="/">the extension</a>,
      or read what <a class="text-white/70 underline decoration-line-hi underline-offset-4 hover:text-white" href="/pro">Pro would add</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
